{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I, behold I, am bringing, etc.</b> The word ״וַאֲנִי״ is far-fetched [grammatically difficult]. And Rashi explained: I am ready to agree with them, etc., [quoting the verse] ״מָה אֱנוֹשׁ״ and so on — end of quotation. And according to what I explained above (Genesis 6:11), that the destroyers filled the earth and were prepared to destroy, HaShem informed that He agrees to permit them to complete the matter. And although here there is only the goal of bringing the flood, go out and learn what they said in the holy Zohar concerning the splitting of the destroyers, for there they were and were found."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The quotation from Rashi references his comment on this verse citing the words ״מָה אֱנוֹשׁ״ — this appears to allude to Rashi's broader argument rather than a direct verse citation; rendered as the Or HaChaim quotes it."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:39:45.360482777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}